# Lead CSVs hold third-party phone numbers for people who are not our
# customers and have not opted in. They must never enter git history.
#
# Machaxi's repo is kept private forever because its history holds member
# names and phone numbers, and purge-pii-history.sh exists because removing
# them after the fact is a separate, painful job. The cheap version of that
# lesson is this file.
#
# The leads live in Postgres (sales.leads, operator-only, in a schema
# PostgREST does not expose). The CSVs are working files — keep them in a
# scratch directory, not here.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
master*

# Which tenants can and cannot carry a reference, with the usage figures
# behind that call. This repo is PUBLIC, and a table stating that a named
# client has almost no students on our product is their commercial
# information — findable by them, and worth less to us than it costs.
# The operating rule ("name only Raj Sports and Gen Alpha") lives in
# WHATSAPP-KIT.md; the evidence stays here, locally.
REFERENCES-INTERNAL.md
